---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout lang="en" title="Privacy Policy | BrewMind" description="BrewMind's privacy policy: the app keeps everything on your device, with no account and no cloud.">
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-28 pb-20 px-6">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p>
        This is a translation of the German original. In case of doubt, the
        <a href="/datenschutz">German version</a> prevails.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>
        Tegrovio, Dominik Palzer<br />
        Sterntalerweg 65<br />
        40235 D&uuml;sseldorf, Germany<br />
        E-mail: <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>
      </p>

      <h2>2. The short version</h2>
      <p>
        The BrewMind app requires <strong>no account</strong>, no e-mail address and no
        password. Everything you record stays <strong>on your device</strong>. There is no
        cloud, no synchronisation and no server that receives your brew data. As the operator,
        I never see your shots.
      </p>
      <p>
        Personal data is therefore processed in two places only: when you visit this website
        (section&nbsp;6) and when you write to me or join the beta (sections&nbsp;4 and&nbsp;5).
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data inside the app</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you create in the app lives in an SQLite database inside the app's protected
        storage area on your iPhone:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Beans, machines, grinders and the paired scale</li>
        <li>Shots with dose, grind setting, yield, times, temperature, ratio and flow values</li>
        <li>Scale measurements taken during a shot (weight and flow over time)</li>
        <li>Your taste verdict for a shot</li>
        <li>App settings</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data does not leave the device on its own. You can copy a single shot or your
        current history selection to the clipboard as JSON and pass it on yourself. Where it
        goes is your call.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no advertising identifier (IDFA), no ad tracking, no third-party analytics, no
        third-party crash reporting, no location access, and no access to contacts, camera or
        photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Deletion:</strong> Individual shots can be deleted in the app. Uninstalling the
        app makes iOS remove the database and everything in it. Since nothing is stored beyond
        your device, there is nothing on my side left to delete.
      </p>

      <h3>Bluetooth (BLE)</h3>
      <p>
        Connecting a coffee scale is optional; without a scale the app records the shot as a
        timer. Bluetooth communication happens locally between your iPhone and the scale only.
        iOS asks for the &ldquo;Bluetooth&rdquo; permission for this. No data is forwarded to
        the internet over Bluetooth.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Beta participation (TestFlight)</h2>
      <p>
        The app is currently distributed as a closed beta via <strong>TestFlight</strong>, a
        service of Apple Inc. / Apple Distribution International Ltd., Hollyhill Industrial
        Estate, Hollyhill, Cork, Ireland. To send you an invitation, your e-mail address is
        transmitted to Apple and processed there as part of TestFlight.
      </p>
      <p>
        Apple provides me with aggregated figures on installations, sessions and crashes of the
        beta build. That analysis is performed by Apple; it gives neither Apple nor me access
        to the contents of your app database.
      </p>
      <p>
        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (performing the test relationship at your request). For
        details on Apple's processing see
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">apple.com/legal/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contact by e-mail</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>, for example
        to sign up for the beta, I process your e-mail address and the content of your message
        in order to reply. Your message is stored with my e-mail provider. I delete the
        correspondence once it is no longer needed and no statutory retention period applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where beta participation is concerned, otherwise
        Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering enquiries).
      </p>

      <h2>6. This website</h2>
      <h3>Hosting</h3>
      <p>
        This website is served via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub Inc., 88 Colin P Kelly
        Jr St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, a Microsoft company). When you open the site, your
        browser transmits technically necessary data that GitHub processes in server log files:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address of the requesting device</li>
        <li>Date and time of the request</li>
        <li>Address of the requested page (URL)</li>
        <li>Referrer URL (previously visited page)</li>
        <li>Browser and operating system used</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; the legitimate interest lies in delivering the
        site reliably and securely. GitHub Inc. is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy
        Framework. See GitHub's
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>
        for details.
      </p>

      <h3>No cookies, no tracking</h3>
      <p>
        This website sets no cookies, embeds no analytics or marketing tools and contains no
        forms. The beta contact is a plain e-mail link that opens your mail client.
      </p>

      <h3>Fonts</h3>
      <p>
        All fonts used (Inter, Calistoga, JetBrains Mono) are served from this server. There is
        <strong>no connection to external font servers</strong> such as Google Fonts.
      </p>

      <h3>External links</h3>
      <p>
        This website links to external sites (e.g. GitHub). The respective provider is
        responsible for data processing on those sites.
      </p>

      <h3>Encryption</h3>
      <p>
        This website is served over a TLS-encrypted connection, recognisable by the
        &ldquo;https://&rdquo; in the address bar.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right at any time to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request information about your stored personal data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
        <li>request rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
        <li>request erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
        <li>request restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
        <li>request data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
        <li>object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
        <li>lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, contact <a href="mailto:hello@brewmind.app">hello@brewmind.app</a>.
        The competent supervisory authority is the State Commissioner for Data Protection and
        Freedom of Information of North Rhine-Westphalia
        (<a href="https://www.ldi.nrw.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.ldi.nrw.de</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the app later gains a feature that lets data leave the device, this policy will be
        updated before it ships. Such a feature would not arrive quietly: it would be visible
        in the app and would have its own section here.
      </p>

      <p class="stand">Last updated: August 2026</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
